{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Say to Elazar.</b> The reason for <b>Elazar</b> is either because HaShem did not consider it fitting that the act be done through Aharon, since he is the high priest, or because through Aharon the judgment had already been carried out and those who offered the incense pans had died — HaShem did not wish the gathering up of the pans to be done through him." "<b>And he shall gather up the pans.</b> One needs to know why it says <b>and he shall gather up</b> with a vav, since this is the beginning of the commandment. It appears that the intention is to add to the first matter, which was the swallowing of Korah and his congregation, whereby the children of Israel saw that the matter of Aharon's priesthood had gone out from HaShem. And further, it adds force and strength to the priesthood in the hand of Aharon for all generations: that he shall gather up the pans, etc., and they shall make them hammered plates, etc., and they shall be a sign for the children of Israel, etc., a memorial for the children of Israel, etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:31.897962105Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}